Package: sbom
Title: Create, Read and Validate Software Bills of Materials
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("James Joseph", "Balamuta", , "james.balamuta@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Create software bills of materials for 'R' packages and
    projects, from installed libraries, package sources, 'renv' lockfiles,
    'Posit Connect' manifests, 'Nix' environments written by 'rix' and
    'Shiny' apps, including the system libraries and bundled code that
    packages carry. Write them as 'CycloneDX' 1.4 to 1.7 documents,
    Software Package Data Exchange ('SPDX') 2.2, 2.3 and 3.0.1 documents or
    Software Identification ('SWID') tags, or as a comma-separated values
    (CSV) inventory, and read bills of materials in these formats from any
    tool. 'CycloneDX' documents and 'SPDX' 2 documents in 'JavaScript'
    Object Notation ('JSON') or 'YAML' are checked against the bundled schema
    of their format, and 'SPDX' 2 documents in Extensible Markup Language
    ('XML') or tag-value form are converted to the 'SPDX' 'JSON' model and
    checked against its schema. 'SPDX' 3 documents are checked against
    their 'JSON' schema, without its Shapes Constraint Language rules, 'SWID'
    tags against structural rules or, when the user supplies it, the
    standard's official schema, and every document against integrity rules
    and the minimum elements of the National Telecommunications and
    Information Administration (NTIA). Optionally, and only on request,
    list the security advisories that Open Source Vulnerabilities ('OSV')
    publishes for the exact versions of the packages.
